{
  "requirement": "A skill that needs a topic whose home under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure` is another skill MUST refer to that skill instead of restating the topic. It MAY summarize the topic in a few lines.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.cli.skill_structure.refer` has two testable obligations. The first is that a skill needing another skill's topic MUST refer to that skill. The second is that it MUST NOT restate the topic. It MAY summarize the topic, and a MAY imposes nothing to check.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_refer_to_a_topic_home_instead_of_restating_it]` covers both obligations for all five bundled skills.\n\n- **Referral:** for each skill, `assert_phrases` reads the whole skill (`SKILL.md` plus its `references/` files) through `bundled_skill`. It asserts that specific referral phrases are present, for example `The habeas skill has the directive and reference syntax`, `\"Choosing references\" in the habeas-requirements skill`, and `following the habeas-evidence skill`. Each skill has between 3 and 6 such phrases. They name the home skill, and sometimes a specific section or reference file.\n- **No restatement:** for each skill, the test loops over every other skill's `home_markers`. These are phrases that state part of a topic in full, such as `A judgment is one of three outcomes`, `## What the review checks`, and `habeas refactor --dry-run`. It asserts that none of them appear in the referring skill's text.\n- **Markers are real:** `assert_home` checks that each home skill actually contains its own markers, so the negative check is not vacuous. It also checks that no other skill contains them. The negative check does not depend on `assert_home`, because it runs inside the subject's own test.\n\nThe restatement check samples characteristic phrases, so it cannot catch every possible paraphrase of a topic. Natural-language text can only be checked this way, and the markers span each home's main topics. I count this as adequate coverage rather than a gap. The only conditional behavior, a phrase being absent or present, is asserted directly.",
  "references": "6115c62c4b082726b08c9d70071d703ebc910924401de32d17d18c54548601b3",
  "inputs": [
